@@ -162,3 +162,17 @@ inconsistent variance/activity flags. All four native gmap checks and three
 installed consumers passed; gbayes' analytic variance and objective checks are
 recorded in its provenance file. The existing marginal-PIP route was unchanged;
 its pinned sblr comparison was not rerun for this adapter-only extension.
+
+## qgg-compatible marginal grouping
+
+`make_qgg_marginal_sets()` implements qgg CS2/CS3 grouping without a qgg
+runtime dependency. It fixes initial lead/member ordering, requires strict
+squared correlation greater than the supplied cutoff, accepts neighborhoods
+meeting the current marginal-PIP target, and removes the entire accepted
+neighborhood from subsequent grouping. CS3 uses initial LD-squared weighted
+PIP order. Input PIPs below the cutoff are excluded. The grouping target is
+expected active-marker count, not component credible coverage.
+
+This implementation follows `qgg/R/genomic_bayes.R::crs`; its GPL-3 source
+provenance is retained in `src/credible_sets.cpp`, alongside the existing
+GPL-3 notices. R callers receive the existing labelled native set diagnostics.
