@@ -228,3 +228,19 @@ No new simulation, eigensystem format, R binding or batch scheduler is needed.
 The [native overview](native-workflow.md) summarises the canonical workflow and
 current limits. The [evaluation record](fine-mapping-evaluation.md) preserves the
 original four-scenario findings and the subsequent baseline convergence correction.
+
+## Full dense LD preparation
+
+`PreparedRegion::from_dense_ld()` and `from_dense_reference()` validate full
+regional correlation and preserve it in marker space. An installed gsolve
+dense Cholesky inverse checks positive definiteness without creating a full
+eigensystem. No jitter, PSD repair or rank truncation is applied. Dense
+retention accepts full rank and mass one only; its minimum eigenvalue is
+unavailable. Singular LD can use the existing explicit positive-eigenmass
+route instead.
+
+Binding uses marker sums of squares to construct dense cross-products for
+the existing gbayes sampler. Caller identity, allele alignment and in-sample
+normalization checks remain enforced. Prepared-fit results separately record
+sampling and posterior-grouping seconds. The R consumer additionally measures
+LD decoding/product, preparation and binding.
